<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    DELIBERATELY DEPENDENCY-FREE. No PackageReference and no ProjectReference:

      * tools/package.ps1 THROWS on any file in the agent publish output that is not named
        KotorCoop.*, because that is the rule the uninstaller uses to decide what it owns.
        A Steamworks.NET or Facepunch.Steamworks package reference would drop a foreign
        assembly there and break the release zip. So the ~8 flat-API entry points we need
        are bound by hand (SteamNative), which costs less than it sounds and keeps the
        published file list to KotorCoop.Steam.dll alone.

      * steam_api64.dll is NOT bundled. Valve licenses the Steamworks redistributable to
        partners shipping on Steam, not to mod authors, and the Steam client itself does not
        contain a copy to borrow. The player supplies it or the whole feature stays inert.

    See docs/research/steam-support.md §§10-11.
  -->

</Project>
